<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Surge.xml                        UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M2 build pass

  miasma_kit_spec.md M2: "RUT_Surge IncidentDef (category ThreatSmall-
  adjacent weighted only into this biome) firing RM_GameCondition_
  GradientSurge". Ban #4 ("no clockwork tide"): this def carries NO
  period/schedule field of any kind (no mtbDays, no mtbDaysByBiome) - a
  linter/grep of this file for either name should find nothing, which is
  the point.

  category=Misc, not ThreatSmall: this repo already has an established
  pattern for "an incident that must NEVER be rolled by the Storyteller's
  own periodic category queue, only fired manually on the mod's own timer" -
  RUT_ContagionProbe.xml and RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak.xml both use Misc for
  exactly this reason. "ThreatSmall-adjacent" (the spec's own phrase) reads
  as describing this incident's TONE/threat-level, not literally wiring it
  into vanilla's ThreatSmall Storyteller comp - doing that WOULD reintroduce
  a schedule (however indirect) this ban explicitly rules out, and there is
  no fixed-cadence field on IncidentDef to set regardless (verified against
  the live decompile's IncidentDef - it has no such field at all; periodic
  incident cadence is entirely a StorytellerComp-side concept).

  workerClass=RimWorld.IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition: vanilla's own
  "create a GameCondition with a random Duration from durationDays, register
  it, send a letter" worker (confirmed real, RimWorld/
  IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition.cs) - no bespoke IncidentWorker subclass
  needed for the firing side at all.

  The actual firing: RM_MapComponent_GradientAxis.TickSurgeRoll (on every
  Miasma map, once per RM_GradientSurgeExtension's own baseMtbDays/
  stormMtbMultiplier roll) manually builds IncidentParms via
  StorytellerUtility.DefaultParmsNow(category, map) and calls
  incidentDef.Worker.CanFireNow(parms) then .TryExecute(parms) - the same
  manual-fire pattern this repo's src/RimUtinni/EmpirePursuit/Source/
  RuthlessPursuingMechanoids.cs:741 already uses
  (IncidentDefOf.RaidEnemy.Worker.TryExecute). CanFireNow still runs (not
  bypassed) so allowedBiomes below and the "already active"/"can coexist"
  checks IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition.CanFireNowSub provides are real
  gates, not just documentation.

  durationDays 0.1667~0.3333 = 4-8 in-game hours (spec's own INVENTED
  ramp-in figure, converted to the days unit IncidentWorker_
  MakeGameCondition.TryExecuteWorker actually consumes) - this IS the
  ramp-in duration RM_GameCondition_GradientSurge.Init() reads back via its
  own inherited Duration property; not re-picked or duplicated there.

  allowedBiomes=[RUT_Miasma]: "weighted only into this biome" (spec's own
  words) - and IncidentWorker.CanFireNow enforces this even on a manually
  built IncidentParms (verified against the live decompile).

  MayRequire is load-bearing even though workerClass itself is vanilla:
  gameCondition points at RUT_GradientSurge, which IS MayRequire-gated on
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards (its conditionClass lives there) - without
  this def carrying the same gate, a mod list missing that mod would leave
  this IncidentDef's gameCondition field pointing at a def that was silently
  discarded, a dangling cross-reference rather than a clean absence.
-->
<Defs>

  <IncidentDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_Surge</defName>
    <label>the breath-tide surge</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimWorld.IncidentWorker_MakeGameCondition</workerClass>
    <gameCondition>RUT_GradientSurge</gameCondition>
    <durationDays>0.1667~0.3333</durationDays>
    <allowedBiomes>
      <li>RUT_Miasma</li>
      <!-- MIASMA_RM_MOD_BUILD_1: second op alongside the frozen twin above -
           the live campaign world still carries RUT_Miasma-painted tiles
           until the terminal paint, and this def now physically lives in
           mandrake.rm.miasma, so both defNames must stay listed for the
           surge to keep firing on the live save AND on a freshly generated
           RM_Miasma tile. -->
      <li>RM_Miasma</li>
    </allowedBiomes>
    <letterLabel>The breath-tide surges</letterLabel>
    <letterDef>NegativeEvent</letterDef>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
